licy for API Artifact\nDescription: You can now validate incoming request messages against an OpenAPI 3.0 Specification using API validation policy. This policy supports validation of the request body (limited to application/json), headers, and query parameters for incoming request messages.   See: API Validation\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-17\nValid as Of: 2024-06-17\nVersion: 2404\n\n--- Record 2757 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Edge Integration Cell now supports outgoing connections through a proxy.\nDescription: You can now route outgoing connections through a proxy. This is useful if your Edge Integration Cell is part of a network using an HTTP proxy.  See: Adding an Edge Node\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-17\nValid as Of: 2024-06-17\nVersion: 2404\n\n--- Record 2758 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Kubernetes cluster deployment on Red Hat OpenShift\nDescription: You can now deploy your Kubernetes cluster on Red Hat OpenShift.  See: Prepare for Deployment on Red Hat OpenShift (OCP)\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-17\nValid as Of: 2024-06-17\nVersion: 2404\n\n--- Record 2759 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Regenerate your credentials for Edge Integration Cell\nDescription: You can be prepared for an upcoming feature by knowing that we have introduced an internal mechanism within Edge Integration Cell.  Once this feature is released, the Edge Integration Cell will convert inbound certificate authentication scenarios into local authentication scenarios, minimizing the runtime dependency on the SAP Business Technology Platform (BTP). We kindly ask for your completion of a manual